{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>And for you, then, what shall I do, my son.</b> This verse indicates that Jacob was blessed in the verse ״ויתן לך״ with a complete blessing encompassing body and soul, for grain and wine and the fatnesses of the earth are in their plain sense a blessing of the body, and they allude as well to a blessing of the soul; for if the intent had been only the grain and wine of the seven nations, why would he say ״and for you, then, what shall I do, my son״ — for surely he also blessed Esau with the dew of the heavens and the fatnesses of the earth? Rather, the intent is that he blessed him with a double blessing, of body and of soul, and nothing was left for Esau in peace." "<b>And the fact</b> that it is written ולכה with the addition of the letter heh is to allude to the five sons that Esau had — Eliphaz, Reuel, Jeush, Jalam, and Korah; therefore he said ולכה, that is, 'and for the five sons of yours, what shall I do — I have already given you to him for servants.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:15:37.009656984Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}